<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch May consumer prices rise 2.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch May consumer prices rise 2.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch consumer price index (CPI) rose a provisional 0.3 percent in May from April, giving a 2.2 percent year-on-year rise, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH CONSUMER PRICE INFLATION     May 97    April 97    May 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI pct change		 0.3	  0.0	 -0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year CPI pct change	  2.2	  1.8	  2.0</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		    119.2	118.9	116.6</p>
<p>NOTES - Economists had expected the May CPI to rise between 1.7 percent and 2.0 percent year-on-year.  </p>
<p>EU-HARMONISED DUTCH INFLATION	May 97    April 97    May 96</p>
<p> Year-on-year CPI pct change	  1.7	  1.2	  1.3</p>
<p> Index (base 1996)		    101.9	101.7	100.2</p>
<p>The detailed non-harmonised index figures were:</p>
<p>					    Weighting     May 97  April 97</p>
<p> Food, drink, tobacco			 180     111.5     110.4</p>
<p> Clothes, shoes				  72     100.6     101.7</p>
<p> Rent, heating, lighting		    261     132.7     132.5</p>
<p> Furniture, household appliances etc.    80     107.1     106.9</p>
<p> Medical care				     6     120.5     120.5</p>
<p> Transport, communication		   144     119.6     119.5</p>
<p> Leisure, education			   107     108.7     108.5</p>
<p> Other goods, services			113     118.5     117.7</p>
<p> Consumer taxes, govt. services	    37     153.7     153.7</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 570 8500</p>
